# TT.TICKET_INTERFACE -- expire_status (S-TICKET-021: forces hot with a private "was X for
# N hours" text; three elapsed-time renderings 2.5 / 2 / 0.33 hours; a non-MCC ticket adds
# the 100008 "hot non-MCC" event) and change_status_event_id_out called directly
# (S-TICKET-008..010, S-TICKET-054): open -> deferred with escalate_after_defer (escalation
# status 20, last_deferral_escalated, deferral date), deferred -> hot with p_hot_reason and a
# NULL private text (handleDeferredTransitions: 60001 event + escalation 10; recoverable 60),
# open -> resolved -> open (last_resolved_date, recoverable 101, UX start re-anchored to the
# event date), a pending customer escalation (20) ended by an acknowledge (60102 event),
# a same-status no-op, a Zitadel-only actor, and the NO_DATA_FOUND paths.
#
# After every successful call the step records '<status> <valid-until set|null> <ev set|null>'
# so the OUT event id and the intermediate states are compared, not only the end state.
# The deferral date is a fixed literal; absolute timestamps are never compared (flags only).
#
# Deliberately passes NULL public/private details where Oracle's text builders concatenate
# them (expire_status always passes NULL public details; step 05 passes p_hot_reason with
# NULL private details): Oracle's || treats NULL as '' -- any difference is a finding.
#
# First live run (2026-10-21) found three translation defects, all fixed since (PASS):
#   - NULL details made the whole public/private text NULL (-> S-TICKET-064, COALESCE);
#   - elapsed hours rendered 2.50 / 2.00 / 0.33 where Oracle prints 2.5 / 2 / .33
#     (-> S-TICKET-021 amended);
#   - recoverable_status_id recorded 101 / 11 on tickets without a last public event, where
#     Oracle's NOT (NULL IN (30016)) takes the ELSE branch (-> S-TICKET-065, reproduced,
#     not corrected).
# One scenario artifact: the resolved -> open re-transition of ticket 952314 accumulated a
# timing-dependent resolved_time (Oracle SYSDATE is second-granular, PostgreSQL's
# statement_timestamp() is frozen within the one DO block) -- the call file now sets the
# resolved period to 30 minutes before reopening.
#
# ORA_USER=system: fixtures in stop.company, stop.contact, mss.host, mss.service,
# mss.host2service; TT holds only SELECT on those. Rolled back at the end.
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=expire_status (3 elapsed-time renderings, non-MCC hot event) and change_status_event_id_out (deferred/escalation/resolved/acknowledge paths) on tickets 952310-952316
